## Scripture texts and quoted works

Each carries its own license, recorded with the text. Every translation stored
under `_implant/raw/translations/` holds a `LICENCE.md` stating its
redistribution terms, and a machine-checked rule in the contract requires it.

Public-domain editions (for example the King James Version, Textus Receptus
and the Septuagint) are marked as such. Translations under active copyright
are **not** stored here: they are cited by reference, without reproducing
their text. Clearing a translation happens before ingest, never after.

Quotations from theological works are used as citations under the ordinary
right of quotation, attributed to work, section and edition.
